  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1404.02 Air Dispersion Modeling Analysis",
  "priorExpiration": "1996-12-22",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1404.02 Air Dispersion Modeling Analysis. If air dispersion modeling analysis is selected, the owner or operator shall conduct an air pollution dispersion modeling impact analysis, in accordance with Env-A 606, demonstrating that the concentration of emissions of each RTAP is equal to or below the corresponding AAL at and beyond the compliance boundary.\n\nSource. #6328, INTERIM, eff 8-24-96, EXPIRED: 12-22-96\n\nNew. #6468-B, eff 3-5-97; ss by #7859, eff 4-11-03; ss and moved by #8278, eff 2-4-05 (from Env-A 1406.02); ss by #9601, eff 11-25-09; ss by #12443, eff 1-5-18; ss by #13334, eff 2-3-22 (formerly Env-A 1405.02)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1400.html"
